BirdNet-Behavior
================

BirdNet-Behavior is licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 (LICENSE; the full text is in
LICENSE-UPSTREAM). It is a rewrite of BirdNET-Pi and is built to work with it;
the lineage and credits are in LICENSE and docs/book/about.md.

This file says, in prose, whose work a build contains or fetches, and under what
terms. The licence texts themselves are in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt, which is
generated from Cargo.lock and the files in third_party/ and ships with every
release archive and container image.

Linked into the binary
----------------------

* Rust packages: every package in the build's dependency tree, under MIT,
  Apache-2.0, BSD, ISC, Zlib, Unicode-3.0 and similar licences. Twelve of them,
  the `symphonia` family (audio decoding), are under MPL-2.0 and are used
  unmodified; their source is at https://crates.io/crates/symphonia and
  https://github.com/pdeljanov/Symphonia.
* ONNX Runtime 1.31.0, MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation, linked
  statically through the `ort` crate. Its own third-party notices are in
  THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt.
* DuckDB 1.5.6, MIT, Copyright Stichting DuckDB Foundation, linked statically
  through `libduckdb-sys`, with the libraries it bundles (their licences are
  in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt).

Compiled into the binary as data
--------------------------------

* Species-name translations: the common names of about 7,000 species in 35
  languages, from BirdNET-Pi's `model/l18n/` (Nachtzuster's fork, commit
  88985a3), reduced to the names that are genuine translations. BirdNET-Pi is
  licensed CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, as this project is, and credits the names to
  @patlevin's BirdNET label translations and to Wikipedia; it does not record
  which name came from which, and neither does this repository. Details, the
  per-source checksums and the rebuild command are in
  crates/birdnet-core/data/l18n/README.md.

Embedded in builds that have analytics
--------------------------------------

* The DuckDB `icu` extension, built by the DuckDB project from ICU (the ICU
  licence, text in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt), pinned by sha256.
* The DuckDB `behavioral` extension, from
  https://github.com/tomtom215/duckdb-behavioral (MIT, the same author as this
  project), pinned by sha256.

Served by the web interface from the binary
-------------------------------------------

* htmx 2.0.4, Zero-Clause BSD.
* Inter Tight, Instrument Serif, JetBrains Mono and Noto Sans, Latin and
  Latin-extended subsets, unmodified from the @fontsource 5.3.0 packages, under
  the SIL Open Font License 1.1. Each family's copyright line and the licence
  are in crates/birdnet-web/static/fonts/LICENSES.txt.

Downloaded, not distributed with the source or the archives
-----------------------------------------------------------

* The BirdNET+ V3.0 classifier and labels, "BirdNET+ V3.0 model developer
  preview" (Preview 3, 2026-01-14), by Mario Lasseck, Maximilian Eibl, Holger
  Klinck and Stefan Kahl, DOI 10.5281/zenodo.18247420, licensed CC BY-SA 4.0
  according to that Zenodo record. The installer fetches it from this project's
  `models-v3.0-preview3` release, which holds an unmodified copy, and falls back
  to Zenodo; both are checked against a pinned sha256.
* The BirdNET geomodel, v3.0.2, from https://github.com/birdnet-team/geomodel:
  source MIT; the trained weights CC BY-SA 4.0, according to that repository's
  README at that tag. Mirrored unmodified in the same release, checked against a
  pinned sha256.
* Other classifiers (for example Google Perch v2, as an ONNX conversion hosted
  on Hugging Face) are fetched only when the operator runs
  `birdnet-behavior --install-model`; their terms are their publishers'.
* Species photographs are cached from Wikimedia Commons (and, when enabled,
  Flickr) under the licence each photograph carries, with the attribution that
  licence requires shown beside it.

In the repository only
----------------------

* tests/testdata/Pica_pica_30s.wav is byte-identical (SHA-256 16fe8840...0098)
  to the test recording in BirdNET-Pi's `tests/testdata/` as of Nachtzuster's
  fork at commit 88985a3, a CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 project, and is used under that
  licence. The original recording credit is not recorded there.
* crates/birdnet-integrations/src/testdata/ holds small samples of public API
  responses (eBird, MET Norway) kept as test fixtures. They are not in any
  release archive.

